      "writtenOn": "2025-01-15T09:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am afraid of such changes in default settings as we have so many diffrent models with diffrent stack in field working with servo currently and dont want to break it. \n\nI see two options:\n- you will need to test if this change do not break compatibility with much more platforms then only Brox \n- if thats only for specific testing maybe that would be possible to implement it via servo command, similiar as you did it here - https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/5980435 . So we do not change default sink pdo but give option to do it when needed for testing",
      "revId": "9479d377ace2ec9bf8b0628b4f84209f1cbc2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f4dacfad_3b162d7b",
        "filename": "board/servo_v4p1/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1548775
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-16T01:06:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As far as I can tell there\u0027s no support for dynamic sink pdos right now. And the current pd policy is to alway select the default when multiple pdos share the same voltage. So I don\u0027t see anyway to implement a servo command to change to pdo without significantly changing the pd infrastructure. \n\nI\u0027ll see if I can get my hands on a few more DUTs.",
      "parentUuid": "2ee407ad_9f115172",
      "revId": "9479d377ace2ec9bf8b0628b4f84209f1cbc2142",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
